# (#126) A for-in BINDER inside an OBSERVED function, over names the census
# does not name. The binder kinds are decided by four separate arms (the
# save/restore kind, the loop-scoped refusal, the numeric-parameter binder
# and the module-numeric binder) and all four keyed on the whole-program
# flag; under the per-name rule they key on the BINDER's own name, so an
# un-named binder in an observed function compiles exactly as it would in an
# unobserved one -- which is the whole theorem, applied to the one mechanism
# where getting it half-right is a storage disagreement (invariant 14: the
# write lands in the env while the read takes the C variable, or the reverse,
# and the loop silently sums zeros).
#
# `w` is the one named channel; `i`, `s`, `k`, `tot` are named by nothing.
tot is 0.0
define f(k) as:
    local w is k
    local s is 0.0
    for i in range of 5:
        s is s + i
        w is w * 0.5
    tot is tot + s
    return [report of w, s, i]
print of (f of 8.0)
print of (f of 4.0)
print of f"tot {tot}"
